# NetTap — Trivy CVE Ignore List
# Upstream base image CVEs with no fix available from Debian.
# Last reviewed: 2026-03-03
#
# These are accepted risks for v1.0 release. All are in OS-level
# libraries of the Debian 12 (bookworm) base image, not in NetTap
# application code. Re-evaluate when upgrading base images.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Debian 12 (bookworm) OS packages — no fix available
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# glibc: integer overflow in memalign → heap corruption
# Affects: libc-bin, libc6 in python:3.12-slim-bookworm & node:22-bookworm-slim
# Status: "affected" — no patch from Debian
# Risk: Low — requires specific memalign allocation patterns unlikely in our workload
CVE-2026-0861

# zlib: integer overflow in zipOpenNewFileInZip4_6 (minizip API)
# Affects: zlib1g in both base images
# Status: will_not_fix — Debian won't patch; the vuln is in minizip, not core zlib
# Risk: None — NetTap never calls the minizip API
CVE-2023-45853

# SQLite: integer overflow
# Affects: libsqlite3-0 in python:3.12-slim-bookworm only
# Status: "affected" — no patch from Debian
# Risk: Low — SQLite is a transitive dep of Python, not directly used by the daemon
CVE-2025-7458

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Docker CLI plugins copied from docker:29-cli into the daemon image (Go binaries)
# Reviewed: 2026-11-03. Each entry expires, so CI fails again and forces a re-check.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# moby/go-archive v0.2.0 (fixed 0.3.0): arbitrary file write while extracting an archive
# Affects: docker-buildx v0.38.1 — buildx's latest release and its master still pin v0.2.0
# Risk: Low — the daemon never builds images or unpacks archives it didn't create
CVE-2026-17106 exp:2026-12-03

# golang.org/x/net v0.58/v0.59 (fixed 0.60.0): HTTP/2 handling
# Affects: docker-compose 5.6.1 and docker-buildx v0.38.1 in docker:29-cli. compose v5.7.0
#   (2026-11-02) has the fix but no docker:cli image ships it yet; buildx has no fixed release
# Risk: Low — both only talk to the local engine over its Unix socket (HTTP/1.1)
CVE-2026-78669 exp:2026-12-03
